# Pre-commit hook — fast gate. See ./pre-push for the heavier one.
#
# Two jobs: keep commits off the trunk, then format/lint staged files.
#
# Note what is deliberately NOT here: any check on how much uncommitted
# work exists. Nagging at commit time punishes the one action we want
# more of — the 2026-08-02 211-file pile happened because people
# committed too rarely, not too often. That check lives in
# scripts/wip-report.sh and runs from post-commit and the Cursor `stop`
# hook instead.

branch=$(git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD)

case "$branch" in
  main | master)
    if [ "$PHARMAX_ALLOW_MAIN_COMMIT" != "1" ]; then
      cat >&2 <<EOF
[pre-commit] refusing to commit directly on "$branch".

Everything here lands through a reviewed PR, so a commit on the trunk is
either a mistake or about to become an awkward force-push. It also feeds
the failure mode that produced the 2026-08-02 pile: work sitting on main
makes every commit feel like the wrong move, so it stops happening, so
the pile grows.

Move to a branch — your staged and unstaged changes come with you:

    git switch -c <feature-branch>

Then commit again. Nothing is lost by switching.

Escape hatch, for a genuine local-only trunk commit:
    PHARMAX_ALLOW_MAIN_COMMIT=1 git commit ...
EOF
      exit 1
    fi
    echo "[pre-commit] PHARMAX_ALLOW_MAIN_COMMIT=1 — allowing commit on $branch"
    ;;
esac

pnpm lint-staged
